   "text": "This SMILES is my reading of the drawing, and I could not confirm the stereochemistry from it, so every stereocentre is written as the L-amino-acid configuration.\n\nThe molecule is a cyclic peptide closed through a thioether, and I traced it from the thioether round the ring:\n\n1. **Thioether:** a Cys-NH\u2082 amide (C-terminal carboxamide) is S-linked to a CH\u2082C(=O) group, which acylates the next residue.\n2. **First residues:** that residue is 4-carboxyphenylalanine, followed by an N-methyl-lysine.\n3. **Lysine side chain:** the N-methyl-lysine side chain (CH\u2082)\u2084NH forms an amide with the \u03b3-carboxyl of a Glu. That Glu keeps its free \u03b1-COOH, and its \u03b1-NH is acylated by 4-(4-iodophenyl)butanoyl.\n4. **Main chain, continuing round the ring:** Val, Val, Ser, Asn, 5-methoxy-Trp, 4-carboxy-Phe, Lys (free NH\u2082 side chain) and 5-hydroxy-Trp.\n5. **Closing the ring:** the 5-hydroxy-Trp is followed by 4-aminopiperidine-4-carboxylic acid (N-substituted with CH\u2082COOH), then Val, which connects back to the Cys nitrogen.\n\nI could not tell from the drawing whether some centres (for example the 5-methoxy-Trp) are D rather than L. I assigned the L chirality tags by checking each centre's neighbour order against the standard L-amino-acid pattern.\n\nSMILES: NC(=O)[C@@H]1CSCC(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccc(C(=O)O)cc2)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](CCCCNC(=O)CC[C@@H](C(=O)O)NC(=O)CCCc2ccc(I)cc2)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](CO)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2c[nH]c3ccc(OC)cc23)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccc(C(=O)O)cc2)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCN)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2c[nH]c3ccc(O)cc23)C(=O)NC2(CCN(CC(=O)O)CC2)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N1"
